content.thinking:
Excellent. DotNetVerify corrected the previous scout: `BlurSwitchCS.ToggleBlurSwitch` is the class with `Switch()`. And it says the switch state is read out of the WMI event payload `Data[0] & 8`.

But my own reading of the decompile shows something different and more precise:
- `m_bExistRFDevice & 8` → `pInfoData->Data[0]` from IOCTL **0x831020c4** to `\\.\EnergyDrv` — the `&8` is on `DAT_140056160` (a byte from the EnergyDrv GPIO IOCTL), and then OSD choice is based on `Data[0] == 1`.
- `CAMERA_BIT7` = bit 7 of `(local_fb88[0] >> 24)` from IOCTL **0x831020dc** to `\\.\EnergyDrv`.

So there are two things:
(a) The *capability* flag `CAMERA_BIT7` (bit7 of the top byte of GetGpioInfo) read at init from `\\.\EnergyDrv` — determines whether the camera OSD is supported.
(b) The camera *state* used at event time: from IOCTL 0x831020c4 to `\\.\EnergyDrv`, `Data[0]`.

